breaking_changes.Adaptation_method:
To avoid unintended cancellation, do not call callback(false) if you want the async flow to continue and the final callback to be executed. For example, in a waterfall function, replace callback(false) with callback(null) or handle the flow differently. If cancellation is intended, ensure your code accounts for the final callback not being called. Example fix for waterfall:
async.waterfall([
  function(callback) { callback(); },
  function(callback) { callback(null); // instead of callback(false) to avoid cancellation },
  function(callback) { callback(); }
], function(err) { /* this will now be called */ });
